PROJECT 01 - SANDOX 2.0
In our earlier system (Sandbox 1.0), we were depending on an intermediate system called NA Data Hub (NA DH) to get refined data. This created delays and dependency issues because we had to wait for NA DH processing before using the data.
In the new system (Sandbox 2.0), we improved this by removing that dependency completely.

1. data source - data mutilpe data sources:
    MDM (Master Data)
    Shipment
    Media
    Trade Panel (unrefined)
    Both refined and unrefined data are now sourced using APIs instead of storage dependencies.

2. Ingestion Layer (ADF)
    We used Azure Data Factory for ingestion and orchestration.

    ADF pipelines call DD APIs to fetch data
    Data is landed into Azure Blob Storage (Landing Zone)
    Pipelines are scheduled using triggers:
    Media data → daily
    MDM → every 6 hours

    We used:
    Copy Activity (API → Blob)
    Linked Services for connectivity
    Key Vault for storing secrets (SAS keys, credentials)

