High-Level Architecture
Pipeline is mainly divided into two parts:
    1. Master Pipeline → Orchestration layer
    2. File Handler Pipeline → Core processing logic

Master Pipeline - 
here first task is databricks notebook, where it check for current run jobs and available job slot, based on this it will create a list and then it will be passed to the for each activity ADF pipeline.
for loop Calls the File Handler pipeline using Execute Pipeline activity
[This master pipeline is used to control and manage job execution. It first checks how many jobs can run in parallel based on system capacity. Then it selects the next set of jobs from a metadata table based on priority and status.
Once the jobs are selected, it updates their status to ‘in progress’ and sends the job list back to ADF. ADF then loops through this list and triggers the actual processing jobs[file handler].
Overall, it ensures controlled, priority-based, and efficient execution of multiple jobs without overloading the system.]

File Handler Pipeline - 
Step-by-step flow:
🔹 1. File Detection
Checks if new files are available in source location
Uses Get Metadata activity

🔹 2. Loop Through Files
Uses ForEach activity
Processes multiple files dynamically

🔹 3. File Validation
Validates:
    File format
    File name pattern
    File size / structure
👉 If validation fails → move file to error folder

🔹 4. Data Ingestion
Uses Copy Activity
Moves data from source → landing zone (Blob/ADLS)

🔹 5. Processing Trigger
Calls Databricks Notebook activity
Performs:
    Transformations
    Data cleaning
    Business logic

🔹 6. Post Processing
Move processed files to archive folder
Maintain logs (success/failure)

